  'page 122 # cosmological # Roe, 6th September 1993 # Machine-translated from transcription in Bennett notation dated April 1990 # This is plate XX in Newbold, and plate IV in Manly31. Newbold\'s folio number # scheme has this as 67r. # This is the folio Newbold claimed showed an annular eclipse. See also John # Manley\'s 1931 article in Speculum: "Furthermore, I invite the reader to # examine carefully Plate IV and say whether it bears any resemblance whatever # to an annular eclipse." # General description of page: # There is a large circle centered on the page. Outside this circle, in the # NE, SE, SW and NW corners, are four smaller circles. In the center of the # large circle is a square, within which is inscribed another circle, within # which is a star. # From the square, lines radiate out in the N, S, E and W directions. Lines # come in towards the square from the perimeter of the large circle in the NE, # NW, SE and SW direction. Each of these eight lines are terminated with a # branching broccoli-like structure. # The small circles in the corners contain between one and four human faces, # joined by lines. # There is a "sentence\'\' of Voynich text above, below, to the left and the # right of the large circle. The bottom left small circle contains a "word\'\' # of Voynich text. # # Labels in upper left and right circles': 'page 122 # cosmological # Roe, 6th September 1993 # Machine-translated from transcription in Bennett notation dated April 1990 # This is plate XX in Newbold, and plate IV in Manly31. Newbold\'s folio number # scheme has this as 67r. # This is the folio Newbold claimed showed an annular eclipse. See also John # Manley\'s 1931 article in Speculum: "Furthermore, I invite the reader to # examine carefully Plate IV and say whether it bears any resemblance whatever # to an annular eclipse." # General description of page: # There is a large circle centered on the page. Outside this circle, in the # NE, SE, SW and NW corners, are four smaller circles. In the center of the # large circle is a square, within which is inscribed another circle, within # which is a star. # From the square, lines radiate out in the N, S, E and W directions. Lines # come in towards the square from the perimeter of the large circle in the NE, # NW, SE and SW direction. Each of these eight lines are terminated with a # branching broccoli-like structure. # The small circles in the corners contain between one and four human faces, # joined by lines. # There is a "sentence\'\' of Voynich text above, below, to the left and the # right of the large circle. The bottom left small circle contains a "word\'\' # of Voynich text. # # Labels in upper left and right circles',
  'otararain # Above large circle': 'otararain # Above large circle',
